  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY THROUGH SUNDAY/...\nIssued at 1258 AM MDT Mon Oct 26 2026\n\nWarm and dry through the rest of the week. Temperatures will \ncontinue to reach into the high-60s to low-70s each day over the \nplains and 50s in the valleys, with generally mild weather across \nthe region. \n\nOur next pattern change will arrive around this weekend. A broad \nupper trough and associated low pressure system will amplify over \nthe Pacific Northwest, digging south and moving onshore by Saturday. \nFlow aloft over our area will turn southwesterly, bringing in more \nmoisture to the mountains, and then possibly the rest of the CWA as \nwell. There still is a lot of deviation between model solutions, so \ntime will tell how impactful the system will actually be for our \narea. We should see a decent chance at some more widespread \nprecipitation, and hopefully more snow for the mountains.",
